    "narrative": "For tonight\u2019s slate, **Jonathan Aranda** stands out as our premier start with a score of 70.47. He draws a highly favorable matchup against Bieber, whose 5.10 xERA signals prime hitting conditions. Aranda\u2019s efficiency is boosted significantly by a +19% SP skill adjustment and a +12% platoon advantage, firmly anchoring him at the top of our lineup. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a high-floor play at 65.73; while he faces a tougher arm in Bradley, his ability to capitalize on base-stealing opportunities against a slower-to-the-plate delivery keeps his value robust. **Gleyber Torres** also trends well at 60.27, despite the volatility of a pending lineup; we are banking on the assumption he leads off, which provides the necessary volume to outweigh the moderate drag from his platoon splits.\n\nThe optimizer\u2019s most difficult exclusion was **Gavin Sheets**, who finished just shy of our \"Strong\" threshold with a score of 37.93. Despite an elite BvP history against Sale, the matchup against a high-tier lefty was simply too prohibitive, forcing us to prioritize the daily efficiency of players like **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Masyn Winn**. Perdomo offers a solid 58.07, leveraging his position in the #3 hole, while **Masyn Winn** is an interesting case; although his base projection is modest, the high probability of a stolen base against Pfaadt keeps him in the lineup. We are closely monitoring the status of **Gleyber Torres** to ensure he stays in the top spot; if he shifts down the order, his efficiency score will likely dip, though no current bench option\u2014with **Cal Raleigh**, **Bryce Harper**, and **Will Smith** all unavailable\u2014offers a high-upside alternative to swap in.",
